Resources and Personnel:

Hardware
This project will require a sizable compute and token budget.
Self-development and continual learning means agents will eventually run continuously for weeks to months.
Exploration is also inherently a highly variable process.
To reliably establish an improvement to performance, we will need to perform several long runs of competing models over many seeds
(e.g., [link: globo project page][text 6 seeds reveal reliable improvement of FTN-M2E over M2E]).
For a point of reference, the experiments done for this proposal used no more than 12 GPUs at any point.

Personnel
AI coding has been indispensible for moving quickly and incorporating modules.
Interfacing the original Dreamer code with a new environment used to take days.
Now it takes 5 minutes.
The role of humans has therefore moved away from coding and toward the insightful thinking that AI coders still cannot do.

My priorities for building a team thus include reseachers that can overcome theoretical obstacles, thinking broadly but practically about the core uncertainties of the project. In particular, FTN is based on a broad picture of how many cortical motifs likely interact, translated into machine learning.
That is the level of translation that I will look for in candidates. Second, I may need engineers with specific industry domain experience, e.g., post-training language and video models. 
Bleeding-edge areas of machine learning in the industry still require human expertise over agentic coding.
In 2027, I aim to hire a minimum of 2, maximum of 6 people.
A team of 3 or 4 can move very quickly and coordinate tightly, with a couple extra spots for headroom as the project expands in its first year.

I am also interested in having rigorous but high-level neuroscience input: What does the brain do generally? What does cortical and hippocampal activity actually look like, compared to what our models do?  
FTN is based on a broad picture of how many cortical motifs likely interact, translated into machine learning.
That is the strategy that will work best going forward.
I anticipate productive collaboration with Astera's Neuroscience team on these questions.
 






